WEBVTT

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:23.870
<i>Everyday I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:31.210
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:38.940
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:45.020
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.800
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:57.570
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:04.540
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:12.480
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:20.150
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.330
Don't play games
with me.

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:43.300
Give me the key to the outside
stairs. Make it fast!

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:47.530
The wind's blowing over 20 meters
per second outside.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.470
You'll be risking
your life!

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.210
Wait! Calm down!

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:00.950
Help me!

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.710
Help me!

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:08.720
Hurry, mister!

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:21.330
But, Detective, it's out
of our jurisdiction.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:24.300
Wait and see.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:25.310
Great!

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:25.970
Great!
What?

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:28.050
You can't carry out
the rescue!

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:30.810
What are you saying?
Huh?!

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:37.650
I understand what
you're saying.

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:40.250
Yes. I'm aware it's outside
our jurisdiction.

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:44.090
Tokuno just called in.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:47.590
Bokuto Station is going to
handle the whole thing.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.560
Everything! All of it!

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:54.730
FILE. 35
FRIENDSHIP AT
250 METERS

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:58.340
Hey! Contact that helicopter
and tell them to land!

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:03.310
And tell them they shouldn't
be taking stupid risks!

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.680
Detective Tokuno!

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.620
Detective Tokuno!
Hello. The cavalry has arrived.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.150
Sorry it took so long.

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:12.050
Sorry it took so long.
Nakajima! I need your help right away.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:13.550
Huh?

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:36.980
The wind's too strong
up here!

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.050
Sorry, kid.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:42.680
If only I hadn't twisted
my ankle.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:46.410
It was that fall
that got me.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.930
Umm... there's an outer
stairwell, isn't there?

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:53.330
Yeah, but we can't get
to it from here.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:57.490
Anyway, the stairs from the observation
deck are on the outside of the tower.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:01.160
You'd be blown off
in an instant.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.600
The helicopter's
gone, too.

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:08.410
Yes, it is.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:13.880
Hey, did you know that the Tokyo
Tower is made of tanks?

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:15.780
It is?

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:18.420
Yeah. American tanks.

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.420
No way.

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:24.930
He twisted
his ankle?

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:27.530
That's what it looked like, from
up in the helicopter.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:33.430
That explains why he hasn't
tried to get inside.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.940
What a mess.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.480
Give me a weather update.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:40.640
A big low pressure system's coming in.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:47.050
They predict wind speeds of
up to 30 meters per second.

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:50.080
That's practically
a typhoon!

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:56.590
Calm down!

00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:01.390
30 meters per second. And the
gusts will be much stronger.

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:05.540
They'll be blown
right off.

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:13.270
The elevator! The elevator's
our only chance.

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:21.650
A long time ago, there
was a war in Korea.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:26.820
After the war, there were lots of tanks
that were no longer needed.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:30.380
Those tanks were taken apart, and
used to make this steel frame.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:36.030
This is made of
tanks, huh?

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.730
Yeah. Pretty amazing, huh?

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:42.640
You should tell your
friends about it.

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:44.730
What is it?

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:47.070
I don't have any
friends.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:51.080
I'm the only one in the Tokyo
Investigation Club.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:53.520
I don't have any friends down there.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:56.390
That's enough.

00:05:57.020 --> 00:06:00.660
I lied to you, mister.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.630
I know.

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:07.690
Nobody on the lower observation deck
had the same badge as you.

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:13.130
There was only one other
kid at the tower today.

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:17.270
But it doesn't matter.

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:21.650
Sure it does! I don't want
to be by myself!

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:28.110
Friends aren't that easy
to come by, you know.

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:33.110
Sometimes you have to search for your
whole life to find a real friend.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:36.860
Is that true?

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:41.620
Yeah. That's been
my experience.

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:46.200
It's the same with your career.
One day you'll find it.

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:57.350
What's keeping that
repair man?

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:00.920
No kidding. Well, I know
he's on his way.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.820
He must be caught in
traffic somewhere.

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.960
There aren't any problems here.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:08.320
You sure have a knack for mechanics.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:11.390
No, not really. Natsumi, can
you pass that to me?

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:14.160
Sure thing.

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:18.700
Nakajima here.

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:20.170
Any changes up there?

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:22.470
No, sir. Nothing to report.

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:24.610
Roger. Keep it up.

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:32.410
It's freezing up here. I can't
believe it's actually June.

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:36.220
Hey, how about some
coffee up here?

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:40.520
Guess I'm out
of luck.

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:46.590
Where's that bloody
rescue team?!

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:50.390
Well, sir, we keep trying
to get them...

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:53.530
...but apparently they're bogged
down with other emergencies.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:55.470
I know that.

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:56.440
Pardon?

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:58.140
I said I already know that!

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:00.010
Yes, sir!

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:03.480
Damn. That was
unlike me.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:07.480
Hang on up there.
Don't give up.

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:12.550
"Current Wind Velocity"

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:16.550
Look! The wind velocity's up
to 28 meters per second.

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:29.470
Why won't it work?

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:31.200
Natsumi.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:33.800
Go to the temple and talk
to Detective Tokuno.

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:36.400
See if you can come up
with another plan.

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:38.610
Do you mean?

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:41.680
No. I'll definitely get this thing
working. However...

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:46.550
...there's no room for error. We
should have backup plans.

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:48.390
You're right.

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:51.190
Good luck,
you guys!

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:00.540
Here it comes!

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:02.560
Here it comes!
This is all my fault! I'm sorry!

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:08.770
Forget it. Who knew that going to Tokyo
Tower could be so exciting?

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:11.710
Can I ask you
something?

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:13.440
Huh?

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:20.260
Hmm?

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:23.890
What?!

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:27.000
What are you doing up here?!

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:29.330
What do you mean?

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:33.830
I brought your coffee. You
ordered some, didn't you?

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:36.900
Yeah, thank you.

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:40.110
Bye.

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:45.110
Huh? Hmm...

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:48.210
I can't go back
down!

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:50.120
Oh, no!

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:54.590
What did you want
to ask me?

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:59.630
I was wondering what you were doing,
all alone at the observation deck.

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:02.260
Huh?

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:04.990
Don't ask such silly questions,
at a time like this.

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:28.020
Hang on,
kid!

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:32.700
Ow! Your coffee!

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:34.290
Ow! Your coffee!
Nakajima here!

00:10:34.470 --> 00:10:36.330
What is it? Come
in, Nakajima!

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:38.660
Oh, no! Is he
all right?

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:40.200
No! He's not going
to make it!

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:41.440
Wait! He's hanging on!

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:43.530
Wait! He's hanging on!
What?! Slow down, Nakajima!

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:58.990
Excuse me, sir.

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:00.390
What is it?

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:03.420
What is it?
I was told to report to Shiba Zojoji Temple.

00:11:04.030 --> 00:11:05.000
Hmm?

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:12.270
"Toyoma Prefectural Police Mountain
Search and Rescue"

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:52.300
Get going!

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:54.770
Yes, sir!

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:02.380
The extremely strong winds today are
wreaking havoc at the Tokyo Tower.

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:05.120
No! Don't take
my bike!

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:08.620
It cost me a fortune!
It's brand new!

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:12.260
You'll get it back! I just need
it to rescue some people.

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:19.200
No!

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:32.680
Who is that guy?

00:12:34.150 --> 00:12:35.820
Shouji Toukairin.

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:36.850
What's his background?

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:37.820
Who knows.

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:38.990
You don't know?!

00:12:38.990 --> 00:12:41.180
Detective Tokuno told me to go with him.

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:42.160
Ready?

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:44.250
Yeah, let's go.

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:56.370
Don't hurt my bike!
I'm begging you!

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:13.460
It's up to us now. Think you
can climb up there?

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:36.200
That guy just
doesn't quit!

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:42.310
Huh?

00:13:42.490 --> 00:13:45.350
I'm not up here for the
view, you know!

00:14:13.180 --> 00:14:15.520
He waited for me.

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:37.880
Are you all right?

00:14:37.880 --> 00:14:39.430
Are you all right?
Maybe not.

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:44.110
Don't say that! What am
I supposed to do?

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:45.840
I wonder.

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:47.690
Don't fall asleep!

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:49.880
I'm not. This is as wide
as my eyes get.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:51.720
Forgive me for having
beady little eyes.

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:52.880
Oops.

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:13.510
Oh, no! My radio!

00:15:22.090 --> 00:15:25.210
"Current Wind Velocity"

00:15:25.620 --> 00:15:27.210
Oh, no!

00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:35.760
"Stairway Closed
Keep Out"

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:43.240
They've signaled! They've made it
to the lower observation deck.

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:46.240
<i>Just another 100</i>
<i>meters to go.</i>

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:12.970
From here on up, it's a narrow
stairway on the outside.

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.600
Right.

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:30.890
Hey, mister.

00:16:30.890 --> 00:16:32.820
Hmm?

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:35.390
Aren't you going to answer
my question?

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:37.260
What question?

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:39.820
Grown-ups are so sneaky.

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:45.100
My question about what you were doing
up here all alone in the first place.

00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:48.600
Oh, that. Well,
it's like this.

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:10.430
You okay?

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:12.920
Th... thank...

00:17:13.030 --> 00:17:13.500
Thank...

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:15.470
Hurry!

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:24.200
<i>Tsujimoto. I know</i>
<i>you can do it.</i>

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:26.940
<i>Make it to the top.</i>

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:08.180
They've made it to
the top deck!

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:10.480
Nakajima!

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:12.260
Huh?

00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:14.160
Me, too!

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:16.820
Let me see, too!

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:18.960
Oh, sure.

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:46.720
Hey, what is that?

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:48.860
Sparks from a blowtorch.

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:51.330
They're trying to rip
apart the door.

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:52.760
You mean!

00:18:52.930 --> 00:18:56.370
Yep. It looks like they've
come to save us.

00:19:09.150 --> 00:19:11.110
Chief!

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:16.180
Hang on to the rope!
I'm going out!

00:19:16.350 --> 00:19:20.520
Tsujimoto! What are
you doing here?!

00:19:21.530 --> 00:19:23.490
I came to save you.

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:30.820
All right. Go for it!

00:19:36.310 --> 00:19:38.270
Get down!

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:43.350
Give me some slack!

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:46.180
Give me some slack!
No! We need to do this slowly!

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:50.490
Come on! We don't
have much time!

00:19:50.650 --> 00:19:52.620
Help me!

00:19:54.390 --> 00:19:56.150
Get over here, Tsujimoto!

00:19:56.590 --> 00:20:00.090
I will! Hurry and give
me some slack!

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:02.360
Here goes!

00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:12.640
Tsujimoto!

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:13.700
Natsumi!

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:15.850
Tsujimoto!

00:20:58.490 --> 00:20:59.610
Well...

00:20:59.720 --> 00:21:03.250
The reason I came to the Tokyo
Tower all by myself, huh?

00:21:03.790 --> 00:21:06.760
It's because I just
wanted to come...

00:21:06.860 --> 00:21:11.030
...and look over the land my officers and
I work hard to serve and protect.

00:21:12.340 --> 00:21:16.500
But that's just between us.
Don't tell anybody, now.

00:21:17.010 --> 00:21:18.840
Why not?

00:21:19.010 --> 00:21:20.530
Because...

00:21:21.180 --> 00:21:23.670
It sounds mushy.

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:26.110
Yeah, I guess.

00:21:32.420 --> 00:21:34.390
Hmm?

00:21:55.750 --> 00:22:01.250
<i>Every time I fall</i>
<i>out of love...</i>

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:11.860
<i>... everything that I see</i>
<i>turns monochrome.</i>

00:22:12.460 --> 00:22:18.760
<i>We often used to go see the</i>
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:18.870 --> 00:22:28.880
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:28.950 --> 00:22:42.830
<i>Even after you've gone, I still wanna</i>
<i>tell the world what it is that I love.</i>

00:22:43.130 --> 00:22:51.070
<i>Looking up to the sky, I try</i>
<i>holding back the tears.</i>

00:22:51.130 --> 00:22:58.910
<i>Flags were moving in the wind and</i>
<i>things seemed brighter yesterday.</i>

00:23:02.910 --> 00:23:04.450
<i>Looking up to the sky, we used</i>
<i>to talk about our dreams.</i>

00:23:09.450 --> 00:23:17.320
<i>No matter how far out of reach they seemed,</i>
<i>dreams could come true, or so it felt.</i>

00:23:17.730 --> 00:23:24.800
<i>Tell me that that fire in your</i>
<i>eyes was not a lie.</i>

00:23:26.870 --> 00:23:28.200
"Sleeping Beauty"

00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:30.700
What, Maho's kitten
is gone?

00:23:30.870 --> 00:23:34.440
Yeah! Shou, Yuuta and
I are looking for it.

00:23:34.540 --> 00:23:35.480
Wanna help us?

00:23:35.650 --> 00:23:40.210
Of course! Detective Tokuno
was looking for his kitty, too.

00:23:40.450 --> 00:23:42.350
Oh, no! Maho's!

00:23:42.620 --> 00:23:43.980
Maho's what?!

00:23:44.150 --> 00:23:46.680
Next time, You're Under
Arrest, File 36...

00:23:46.790 --> 00:23:48.360
..."The Lost Kitten."

00:23:48.360 --> 00:23:50.360
I'm coming, Maho!
